# TLA+ model output is regenerated by check.sh. `out/` holds the chart and
# report; `states/` holds TLC's fingerprint and state dumps, which are megabytes
# of binary and must never be committed. check.sh passes -metadir to keep them
# out of the tree, and this is the backstop for a manual TLC run.
#
# The glob is `out/*`, not `out/`: git never descends into an excluded
# directory, so the negation below could not match a path under `out/`.
hack/formal/*/out/*
hack/formal/*/states/

# The drawn chart is checked in so a reader sees the state machine without
# installing a JDK, TLC and bun. It is a deterministic function of the model and
# its view module, so `hack/formal/check.sh all --chart` reproduces it byte for
# byte; the rest of out/ (report, tlc.out) stays regenerated.
!hack/formal/*/out/chart.mmd
